// Template — copy this file to Secrets.xcconfig (already gitignored) and fill in
// your real values there.
//
// These two values are NOT secret — the Supabase anon key is designed to be
// public and embedded client-side, the same way a Firebase config is. The
// real Anthropic API key never goes here anymore; it lives only as a
// server-side secret on your Supabase project (`supabase secrets set
// ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...`), read by supabase/functions/anthropic-proxy.
//
// To get these two values:
//   1. Create a project at https://supabase.com (free tier is enough to start).
//   2. Deploy the proxy: `supabase functions deploy anthropic-proxy` from the
//      repo root (after `supabase login` and `supabase link`).
//   3. SUPABASE_FUNCTION_URL is the deployed function's URL — Supabase shows
//      it after deploy, in the form:
//      https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/anthropic-proxy
//   4. SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is on your project's dashboard under
//      Settings → API → Project API keys → anon / public.
// NOTE: xcconfig files treat "//" as a comment marker (like C++), so a plain
// "https://" here would silently truncate to just "https:" — Xcode drops
// everything after the "//". The "$()" below is an empty build-setting
// reference placed BETWEEN the two slash characters (not just before them —
// they still count as a comment-starting "//" if left adjacent) so the raw
// file never contains a literal "//" for the parser to trip on; it still
// resolves to the full "https://..." URL at build time.
SUPABASE_FUNCTION_URL = https:/$()/your-project-ref.supabase.co/functions/v1/anthropic-proxy
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = your-anon-key-here

// Same project, just its root URL instead of one function's path — used by
// AuthManager.swift (Sign in with Apple / Supabase Auth) and
// CloudSyncManager.swift (the account-sync repository layer) to reach
// Supabase's built-in Auth and PostgREST APIs. Same "//"-escaping caveat as
// SUPABASE_FUNCTION_URL above applies here too.
SUPABASE_PROJECT_URL = https:/$()/your-project-ref.supabase.co

// RevenueCat's public SDK key (starts with "appl_" for an Apple App Store app) —
// also not a secret, safe client-side, same reasoning as the two values above.
// Found in the RevenueCat dashboard under Project Settings → API Keys.
REVENUECAT_API_KEY = your-revenuecat-public-api-key-here

// TelemetryDeck's app identifier (added 2026-08-12) — see
// Services/AnalyticsManager.swift for what this does and doesn't send. Found
// on the TelemetryDeck dashboard (dashboard.telemetrydeck.com) after
// creating a free app there: Project Settings → General → App ID. Not a
// secret with spend/write access, just routed through this file for
// consistency with every other environment-specific value here.
TELEMETRYDECK_APP_ID = your-telemetrydeck-app-id-here

// Google Sign-In (added 2026-08-01), used by AuthManager.completeGoogleSignIn
// as a second sign-in option alongside Sign in with Apple.
//
// Setup, in this order:
//   1. In the Google Cloud console (console.cloud.google.com/auth/clients),
//      create TWO OAuth client IDs for the same project:
//        - one of type "iOS"  → bundle ID com.sustainapp.glp1
//        - one of type "Web"  → this one exists only so Supabase can validate
//          the token; the app itself never opens it in a browser.
//   2. In the Supabase dashboard → Authentication → Providers → Google:
//        - enable the provider
//        - paste BOTH client IDs into "Client IDs", comma-separated, WEB ID
//          FIRST (Supabase's docs are explicit about the ordering)
//        - turn ON "Skip nonce check". This is required for the
//          GoogleSignIn-iOS flow: that SDK does not attach a nonce the way
//          Apple's does, and Supabase rejects the token if it expects one and
//          finds none. This is the single most common reason a correct-looking
//          Google integration returns a 400 from /auth/v1/token.
//   3. Fill in the three values below.
//
// GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID is the iOS client ID, e.g.
//   123456789-abcdefg.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID = your-ios-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

// GOOGLE_SERVER_CLIENT_ID is the WEB client ID from step 1. Passed to Google's
// SDK as the server client ID so the minted ID token is audienced for Supabase.
GOOGLE_SERVER_CLIENT_ID = your-web-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com

// GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID is the iOS client ID with its two dot-separated
// halves swapped — Google shows it directly in the console, and it is also the
// REVERSED_CLIENT_ID value in a GoogleService-Info.plist. It becomes the app's
// custom URL scheme so Google's sheet can hand control back to Sustain.
// No "//"-escaping needed here: this is not a URL, just a scheme string.
GOOGLE_REVERSED_CLIENT_ID = com.googleusercontent.apps.your-ios-client-id
